{"id": "sevt_013bJ1kVJswhbsv9SHygaq31", "content": [{"text": "Confirmed. Each cart request now fires 8\u201316 separate `sku_prices` queries (one per cart line); zero such queries existed before 14:16:47.\n\n## Triage summary \u2014 cart p99 spike ~14:17 UTC\n\n**Evidence**\n- **Metrics:** cart `p99_latency_ms` sat ~76 ms through 14:15, then jumped to ~3,956 ms at 14:16 and climbed to ~5,900 ms by 14:59. `error_rate` stayed near-zero throughout \u2192 a latency regression, not failures.\n- **Deploy lineup:** cart deploy `0c1986c` (frank, \"split price lookup into a loop\") landed **14:16:45**; p99 moves in the 14:16 bucket. Clean fit. The other deploy in-window, checkout `21acf62`, only adds an index `CONCURRENTLY` on a different service \u2014 benign.\n- **Diff:** `0c1986c` replaced a single batched query (`SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id__in=ids)`, grouped in memory) with a per-row `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id=line.sku_id)` inside a `for line in rows` loop. Classic N+1 \u2014 the runbook's #1 recurring cause.\n- **Log confirm:** the per-row query `SELECT * FROM sku_prices WHERE sku_id = ?` first appears at **14:16:47** (2s after deploy), with **zero** occurrences before. It then runs 60\u2013200\u00d7/min, at **8\u201316 queries per cart request** \u2014 the fanout driving the tail latency.\n\nFix: revert `0c1986c` / restore the single batched `sku_id__in` lookup.\n\n> **Root cause:** `0c1986c` \u2014 refactor turned the batched cart price lookup into a per-row query inside a loop (N+1), firing 8\u201316 `sku_prices` queries per request and blowing up cart p99.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:31:05.182765Z", "type": "agent.message"}
